// endpoint_discard_merge.proto — DiscardMerge: end a merge request that
// stands off its queue without landing it. AGENT API section.
//
// It is the ONE way a request ends short of a landing, so it is the one way
// an async merge's merge workspace is closed for a merge that never landed:
// leaving the queue never closes it (RequeueMerge). Discarding an async
// merge's request closes its merge workspace, and removes the worktree the
// request asked to clean up on landing, through git's clean door: a worktree
// holding uncommitted changes is kept. No branch is ever deleted: a discarded
// merge's branch still holds work that never landed. Discarding a workspace's own merge drops only the request: the workspace,
// its worktree and its branch stay as they were.

